      "obligation": "refuter:6:1",
      "id": "lem-the-generic-borel-half-and-opposite-half-form-a-dj-crossed-double",
      "location": "Proof 1.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The proof says to reduce “K_hF_j to q^{-α_j(h)}K_hF_j.” The scoped Drinfeld–Jimbo definition instead gives K_hF_j = q^{-⟨α_j,h⟩}F_jK_h, so the rewrite must move F_j before K_h. With h=h_j, the printed rule forces (1−q^{-2})K_{h_j}F_j=0 and hence F_j=0. The scoped rank-one oscillator example has λ_0=(1+q²)/((q−q^{-1})(1−q²))≠0 and represents F(X^0)=λ_0X^{-1}≠0. The printed rule also leaves the claimed F<K<E inversion count unchanged, so it does not establish the stated normal forms.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "59c20d02ca348b7a715581019d4db628187153b07b63f458f41dfb9bdc541d7c"
    }
